id: pm-brief-nsks
title: Render stakeholder briefs through explicit disclosure profiles
description: "Acceptance: render one brief for internal agents, external reviewers or public sharing with a field-level exclusion manifest. Synthetic secrets and disallowed custom fields never enter public output. Unknown policy fields fail closed. Dry run explains exclusions without echoing forbidden text. Provide typed SDK and native CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, typed refusals with remedies, README and example, non-git public tracker replay, and npm plus Bun CI release gates."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: added,disclosure
created_at: "2026-10-23T15:28:21.049Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T23:09:37.859Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T21:43:41.531Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T17:16:46.000Z"
author: codex-agent
resolution: "Adds explicit stakeholder disclosure profiles, selector-safe field projection and real non-git privacy regressions."
expected_result: "Acceptance: render one brief for internal agents, external reviewers or public sharing with a field-level exclusion manifest. Synthetic secrets and disallowed custom fields never enter public output. Unknown policy fields fail closed. Dry run explains exclusions without echoing forbidden text. Provide typed SDK and native CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, typed refusals with remedies, README and example, non-git public tracker replay, and npm plus Bun CI release gates."
actual_result: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/172, merged 2026-10-23T17:16:46Z, merge cdcd1e3f5e59db8b53cdfa5397e6d1ec18ef080d: Adds explicit stakeholder disclosure profiles, selector-safe field projection and real non-git privacy regressions."
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T15:29:08.533Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against the pinned SDK and sibling package sources: core sdk/context-intent-contracts bounds read projections; pm-github README public import gate owns staged publication; pm-memory README input privacy gate owns mutations/import. This item owns only brief-specific disclosure/rendering. Reuse native PmClient.listAllComplete plus certifyCompleteListResult, existing buildBrief ranking, scanMutationSecrets, estimatePmOutputTokens, native JSON/TOON formatting and expected-error contracts. Policy is a closed audience allowlist with deny-only selectors; unknown policy keys/selectors refuse before reads. Exclusion paths use array indices and opaque ordinals for unknown keys; no source values in dry runs or refusals. Local targeted tests and static gates only; full release checks use the npm/Bun CI matrix at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T15:40:28.236Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: typed SDK renderDisclosureBrief/buildDisclosureBrief/parseDisclosurePolicy plus brief disclose --audience or --policy. Profiles can only narrow. Guard native source fields before compaction, then permitted rendered values; value-free manifests aggregate profile denials and retain ordinal secret paths. Default complete output ceiling 8000 estimated tokens; dry runs contain no brief. Source compaction remains visible. Five behavioural reversions each produced the expected regression failure: credential guard, closed policy keys, dry-run suppression, unknown-field exclusion, and pre-compaction source guard. Each mutant changed only its guard branch, ran the matching node --test --test-name-pattern regression, and was restored byte-for-byte. No SDK mocks. Initial nine targeted tests passed; expanded ten-test suite now adds source-secret and native error coverage."
  "2026-10-23T15:40:29.597Z",codex-agent,"Public-data replay: exported committed public pm-brief tracker at 7172186062a0398ffe585a593f7636a84b847671, excluded extensions, copied into a non-git scratch project and made all tracker files/directories read-only. Certified 91 records and 91 unique IDs. All 3 profiles plus 3 dry runs passed with identical exclusion manifests, no source compaction, and unchanged source/copy fingerprints. Internal: 5549 compact JSON bytes, conservative 4347-token ceiling; external: 4361 bytes/3441 tokens; public: 3274 bytes/2412 tokens. Profile exclusions 0/61/151 respectively; each profile reports one recognized secret-field exclusion and one unknown-field exclusion. No source values or private data are reproduced. The worked replay is docs/examples/disclosure.md."
  "2026-10-23T15:42:31.898Z",codex-agent,"Local verification passed via pm test --run --progress: 10/10 feature tests, zero failures/skips; disclosure.ts 100% lines, 99.15% branches, 100% functions. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint (171 declarations) and git diff --check passed. Updated existing command-registration and renderer-ownership contracts to include brief disclose and preserve native structured output. Two focused host-contract tests passed. Linked-test automatic evidence recording is disabled in project settings, so this comment preserves the measured results without changing policy. Full npm/Bun release checks and packed current/minimum-host acceptance will run in CI; no local full-suite run on the saturated host."
  "2026-10-23T15:44:24.781Z",codex-agent,"PR opened ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/168 . Local strict health separately reported existing merge_fence_drift:2 (the checked-in fence is unchanged from main) and local pm-github extension host-version skew against the pinned SDK. No history drift was reported. Fence ownership remains pm-brief-fence165; owner rules prohibit merge-driver work here. Fresh-clone CI health is the tracked-state evidence. These environment conditions do not alter the passing feature acceptance tests."
  "2026-10-23T15:44:35.475Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding PR reference: the created disclosure PR is https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/pull/172 . The earlier numeric PR reference was a transcription error. Full CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/39980782469 ."
  "2026-10-23T15:47:09.419Z",codex-agent,"Final local integration strengthened: the installed no-git JSON/TOON CLI fixture now contains both a native synthetic credential title and disallowed custom/body text. Both render and dry-run paths omit these markers. The expanded suite still passes 10/10 with 100% lines, 99.15% branches and 100% functions in disclosure.ts. Independent review remains unavailable; evidence is added to existing pm-brief-1oo2 rather than creating a duplicate. No approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-23T15:55:40.452Z",codex-agent,"Overlap refresh also checked the installed current CLI 2026.10.23 public sdk/context-intent-contracts surface: named field-group projections, token/degradation receipts and continuations remain core read contracts; no stakeholder disclosure policy is supplied there. The package continues to use its unchanged pinned 2026.10.20 SDK, with minimum-host acceptance at 2026.10.13. Sibling boundaries and feature ownership remain as recorded in the opening overlap comment."
  "2026-10-23T16:04:19.398Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/39980782469 passed all five jobs at ad8527adbf0b7c6153d7068317281fe485fe85e3. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 423/423 tests with zero failures/skips, 100% lines and functions over all four shipped source files; branches measured 98.28% (npm) and 98.32% (Bun), above the unchanged 97.85% threshold. Each gate passed three packed scenarios (npm current, Bun current, npm minimum), exercising all three disclosure profiles and a dry run. Node 22 and 26 jobs also each passed 423 tests and packed acceptance; Windows audit passed. Fresh-install strict tracker health passed. No merge/release was performed."
  "2026-10-23T16:04:21.850Z",codex-agent,"Final refinement also rejects inherited profiles, hidden own keys and symbol-keyed policy fields; no unknown fields are silently ignored. Updated guard behavioural reversion failed the policy regression as expected, then was restored. Final pm test --run --progress passed all three linked commands: 10/10 feature tests, 2/2 host-contract tests, typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and diff validation. Feature coverage is 100% lines, 99.16% branches, 100% functions. The read-only 91-item public replay was rerun and reproduced every recorded measurement; the worked example now includes its reference results. Final evidence commit will receive fresh CI; the PR body will link that exact-head run. Remaining outside-scope work is preserved in existing pm-brief-fence165 and pm-brief-1oo2. No new core CLI/SDK defects were found. Claim released for orchestrator review; keep the item in progress until independent verification."
  "2026-10-23T16:50:53.848Z",codex-agent,"Reopened implementation work for orchestrator review finding: a literal custom key containing selector punctuation was parsed as a nested allowed field and could enter disclosure output. Remote PR head was pulled first; advanced main was merged with CHANGELOG.md regenerated inside the merge. Fix matching using arrays of exact data-key segments; profile wildcards may match only numeric array indices. Unknown selector-shaped keys must generate ordinal unknown_field exclusions. Add root and nested regression cases for the exact focus.*.title key and dot, wildcard and bracket punctuation; retain passing existing behavior and prove failure with only the matching fix reverted."
  "2026-10-23T17:00:52.296Z",codex-agent,"Fixed selector injection in renderDisclosureBrief: only trusted profile definitions are split into selector segments. Data traversal carries exact string keys and numeric array indices; profile wildcards match numeric indices only. A literal focus.*.title root key, dot/wildcard/bracket keys and object keys impersonating array slots are now unknown_field exclusions with ordinal paths. New regressions: selector-shaped data keys remain unknown field exclusions; object keys cannot impersonate array wildcard segments. The first exercises 13 literal keys independently at root and nested positions across public, external and internal profiles, including identical value-free dry-run manifests."
  "2026-10-23T17:01:09.654Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: saved the fixed disclosure.ts bytes, restored only the pre-fix renderDisclosureBrief function from the merged branch baseline, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"selector-shaped data keys|object keys cannot impersonate\" test/disclosure.test.ts. Both regressions failed with exit 1; the first failing case used public profile and only the literal focus.*.title custom key. New compiled profile metadata/helper and tests remained unchanged. Restored the fixed source byte-for-byte (SHA256 bd32a79bfe2a65860606808383ec868093d2d088b684fb95da1070235a2bfccd). The tests import TypeScript source directly, so this proof did not require a dist rebuild. The same command then passed 2/2 through pm test --run --progress --only-last --timeout 600."
  "2026-10-23T17:01:19.829Z",codex-agent,"Local validation: disclosure suite 12/12 passed, zero failures/skips, including existing no-git installed JSON/TOON and synthetic-secret regressions. Measured disclosure.ts coverage is 100% lines, 99.17% branches and 100% functions. The strengthened two regression tests passed through the newly linked targeted command. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring (171 declarations) and git diff --check passed. Full npm/Bun release gates remain delegated to CI at unchanged thresholds; their exact-head URL and counts will be retained in PR 172. Prior public-data replay and completed feature work were preserved. Claim released for orchestrator verification; do not close the item."
